# A match(_) written as a discriminated-union schema vetted VALID over
# data the selected arm refuses. Run:
#   aontu vet --at '$.Event' match-hole-scrutinee.aontu match-hole-scrutinee.json
# The hole-fill rule puts the peer INTO the call and does not keep it
# as a constraint on the way out -- right for `upper(_) & "hello"`,
# unsound for a schema: the document was consumed selecting the arm
# and then never checked against it, so `total_cents: -5` passed a
# `min(0)` the same run prints in the arm.
# expected: a verdict that does not claim the data was checked
# actual:   verdict: valid, exit 0 (Go)
# FIXED 2026-09-07 -- the call residuates instead, and the run says
# verdict: incomplete with [aontu/conjunct] at $.Event.
Placed: close({ type: "order.placed" total_cents: integer & min(0) })

Event: match(_, { type: "order.placed" }, $.Placed)
